WEBVTT

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.990
<b>Children's Fortress</b>

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.990
<b>Children's Fortress</b>

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.020
Help me!

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:00.130
You planning to kidnap
children too, you gangsters?

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:03.880
We'll fill you full of holes and 
send you back to Kurokawa's!

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.760
Nuts...

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.750
Who is this "Kurokawa"?

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.490
The governor of Imihama.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.140
They say his reelection is guaranteed,

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.400
though that's just because all 
the other candidates went missing.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.040
I dunno where you got that wrong idea,

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.440
but stop pointing weapons at travelers!

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.030
We're just trying to get to Akita!

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.910
Quit lying!

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:30.670
No one heading north would pass
 through the Calvero Shellsand Sea,

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.720
where water and food are scarce!

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.580
Everyone has their own 
reasons for doing stuff, y'know!

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:39.960
Though, yeah, it's true that
 we could use some food.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.220
But we have money, so please spare some.

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:47.220
No way you've got much 
money walking around like that.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.980
Now hurry up and let Kousuke go!

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:52.020
Guess you're in your rebellious phase.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.480
Whatever. Good thing I saved a copy.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.950
<b>Man-Eating Redcap</b>

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.950
<b>Man-Eating Redcap</b>

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.950
<b>Akaboshi Bisco</b>

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.950
<b>Akaboshi Bisco</b>

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.950
<b>Wanted</b>

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.950
<b>Wanted</b>

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.950
<b>Age: 17
Height: 180cm</b>

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.950
<b>on 28 Counts 
of Mushroom 
Terrorism</b>

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.950
<b>800,000 Sol Reward</b>

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:01.940
I'm Akaboshi Bisco, the man-eating 
redcap causing chaos all over Japan!

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:06.810
If you manage to take me to Imihama alive,
you'll get an 800,000-sol reward!

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.070
Hey, wh-what are you doing, Bisco?!

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:11.800
Akaboshi?

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.350
The man-eating redcap, Akaboshi?

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:14.750
The real deal?

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.100
Wow!

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:15.880
Really?!

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.950
See? It all worked out.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:25.220
You call this "working out"?

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.670
The fishermen of Calvero 
always keep their word.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:33.250
We'll give you food, so behave yourselves
until we turn you over to the authorities.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.840
Thank you for looking after us.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.800
What an amazing man.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.120
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.120
<b>Tetsujin Town</b>

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.000
Who are they?

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:55.000
I don't know.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:55.890
Who is it?

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:07.840
This town has kind of a strange shape.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:13.680
It was carved out of a piece of Tetsujin
 that landed here after the explosion.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.670
That's what the adults said long ago.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.020
<b>Liquid Bonecoal</b>

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:24.030
Akaboshi, you go here.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.820
Kousuke, come with me.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:29.600
Plum, you keep an eye on
 White Panda down there!

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:13.460
Thank you so much. You saved our lives.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:18.050
I just happened to be passing by. 
There's no need to thank me.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:24.210
The bandits' trap was still there, wasn't it?

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:25.920
Bandits?

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.940
You mean that pile of corpses?

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:33.250
They used this place as a base 
to attack traders passing through.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.720
Serves 'em right.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.200
Hey, I know.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:40.480
If you like, why don't you come to
 our place? You can fix it up there.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.880
Really?

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:44.580
Yes, it's just up ahead.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:51.230
This is good!

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:54.890
You're exaggerating. 
It's just clams simmered in milk.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:05:59.380
Thank you.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.110
But are you sure?

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:06.270
I had no choice. You looked 
like you were going to drop it.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:12.490
Hey, aren't there any adults here?

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:16.300
You're all armed, too.
Do bandits strike out here?

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:19.830
Schools of flying blowfish rise up in winter.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.180
Flying blowfish?

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:24.440
They eat several people every year,

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.660
and our weapons are getting old,

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:30.450
so we don't know if we'll 
make it through this winter.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.070
Let me see that.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:38.190
I-It's been like this forever.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:41.200
It's not just me. Everyone has it.

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:43.990
It's called Rusting, right?

00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:44.970
Huh?

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:48.500
That's what the Imihama army 
said when they barged in here.

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:53.460
The medicine costs a fortune,
so all the adults left to earn money.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:59.220
That's why they're all forced to wear those 
strange masks by the governor, Kurokawa.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:03.980
<i>Kurokawa? How could he do this to children?</i>

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:11.870
Plum, the disease you all have isn't Rusting.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:13.080
Huh?

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.220
Here you go. Drink up.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:23.880
We used to live in that apartment block.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:27.870
After everyone was gone, we moved here.

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:32.140
What on earth happened here?

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:35.630
A mass outbreak of Rusting.

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.980
I see. Here, too, huh?

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:41.640
It's all his fault.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:43.140
"His"?

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:51.110
Our town was wiped out by a Mushroom
 Keeper who just showed up one day.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:03.290
Around here, we didn't used to fear 
Mushroom Keepers as much as we do now.

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:10.670
He stayed in one of the apartment blocks
and used mushrooms to treat illnesses.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.050
At first, it looked like they 
were definitely doing some good.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:18.850
But then...

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.820
When we investigated later,

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:31.310
it turned out that everyone the Mushroom 
Keeper had given medicine to had Rust all over.

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:34.810
Everyone still alive fled,

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:39.580
and before we knew it, 
it was just the two of us left.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:44.920
Then the Mushroom Keeper 
came to us and said,

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:49.650
"Thank you. That experiment was worthwhile."

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:51.590
<i>That bastard.</i>

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:55.190
<i>So the Mushroom Keepers 
really are spreading Rust.</i>

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:59.200
The two of us came over here after that.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:02.720
We had a lot of memories
 in this place, you see.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:07.820
It was our dream to fix this place up one day.

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:13.280
We hoped that if we did, people 
would return to this town once more.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:19.030
That's why we occasionally pick up 
things we think might be useful.

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:24.030
Like the playground equipment outside, 
which we repaired and improved ourselves.

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:32.370
What the hell?!

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:39.080
You brats get to eat stuff
 this good all the time?

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.660
We're not brats!

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:43.380
We're proud Calvero fishermen.

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:45.330
That was great.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:46.150
More.

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:47.510
Y-You...

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:49.940
Don't you realize the position you're in?

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:56.020
The weapon on that wall over 
there is a pretty nasty piece.

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:58.990
That's my dad's harpoon.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:02.860
He was the best fisherman 
here, and our chief.

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:07.650
He stood up to the Imihama army
 and got his head blown off.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:10.220
It's a great harpoon.

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:15.670
That harpoon and my grudge are 
the two things I never want to rust.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.640
That's why I keep it on display.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.820
Your memories aside, it's a great harpoon.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:22.800
Give it to me.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.410
Wh-What?!

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:26.550
There's no point in putting it on display.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:29.560
A pipsqueak like you would be
 out of your depth wielding it.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.800
It's better if I use it.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:32.810
How dare you?!

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:33.790
Nuts!

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:43.880
All right.

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:17.480
Excuse me.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:18.800
I'd like to ask a question—

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:26.080
Ecchan.

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:29.450
Did that woman drink the tea?

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:31.430
Don't worry.

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:34.370
I sneaked a peek at her cup, and it was empty.

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:38.580
That iron pole of hers was like an oni's club.

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:40.000
Real scary.

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:44.380
Then let's turn that woman 
into a statue of a female oni.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:47.530
Oh?

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:50.450
All done with the repairs to your bike?

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.240
What is this place?

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:54.840
A shelter.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:58.520
It's an ideal dwelling because we 
don't have to worry about Rust here.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:03.170
It appears you two are the ones 
who have been acting like bandits.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:06.770
I can't look the other way 
now that I know you're evil.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:07.790
Die!

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.290
It's starting to work.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:19.050
We put poison in the tea you just drank!

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:22.660
What? How...

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:25.670
The Rust in my chest was 
just aching a bit, that's all.

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:29.870
I'm not so reckless as to gulp down 
tea that might be poisoned.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:32.800
So you two really were 
the ones who set that trap.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:34.050
Shou-chan!

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:38.080
Shou-chan, this way!

00:12:38.630 --> 00:12:39.570
Wait!

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:49.330
<b>EXIT</b>

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:53.570
Ecchan, we might be done for.

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:56.950
I don't think we can beat this woman.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:13:01.090
You might be right. I guess we'll 
just have to go with <i>that</i> plan.

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:06.850
We always talked about how this day 
would probably come sooner or later.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:11.910
The two of us can live 
all by ourselves in here.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:14.510
We won't bother anyone anymore.

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:19.620
In return, we ask you to 
please stop bothering us, as well.

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:21.050
Goodbye.

00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:22.630
What selfish drivel are you—

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:37.130
Nuts!

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:40.120
Hey, Nuts!

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:43.620
What are you all screaming about?!

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:46.690
Look at this, Nuts! My arm!

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:50.380
See? It's completely healed! 
I can move it again!

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:53.470
That White Panda must be 
Buddha or Christ or something!

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:56.360
He healed us all in an instant!

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:58.890
What? Don't be stupid!

00:13:59.390 --> 00:14:02.150
Kousuke! You watch Akaboshi.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:05.710
What?! By myself?!

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.530
<b>Konakidani</b>

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.530
<b>Banryouji Temple</b>

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.530
<b>Line</b>

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.530
<b>Konakidani</b>

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.530
<b>Haebaoka</b>

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.530
<b>Tsurikubisaki</b>

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.530
<b>Hakujadai</b>

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.530
<b>Jizounuki Kouen</b>

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:13.240
That a route map for the train?

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:15.160
Y-You recognize it from there?

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:17.330
Yeah, kinda.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:20.870
When my mentor and I passed through 
Mie from Nara, we took the subway.

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:23.820
I think it was called the
 Keikyuu Benibashi Line.

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:26.180
Huh? You got an abandoned line moving?!

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:27.720
That's incredible!

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.320
Hey, you're a Mushroom Keeper, right?

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:33.300
You're not afraid of Mushroom Keepers?

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:38.830
M-My father once told me that when
 I nearly died from an illness long ago,

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:41.180
it was a Mushroom Keeper who healed me.

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:46.610
So I've always wanted to 
talk to a Mushroom Keeper,

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:48.600
since one of them saved my life.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:51.760
Oh, I know! You're going north, right?

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:54.290
Then take this map with you.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:58.580
I-It has all the subway 
stations in Touhoku on it.

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:02.340
Look, kid. I'm a prisoner, remember?

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:07.080
I've looked at it so much,
 I've got it all memorized.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:12.450
My father always said he wanted to 
repay the Mushroom Keepers one day.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.470
A-And even though my father died,

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:18.220
I can repay the favor for him!

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:22.720
I-I need to go pee real quick!

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:25.730
Hey! Shouldn't you be watching me?!

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:27.590
Please don't run away!

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:32.920
Okay, then...

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:36.480
Wh-What on earth...

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:40.060
It wasn't Rusting afflicting all of you.

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:41.930
It was a simple case of shellskin.

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:45.510
Anyone with an ounce of 
medical knowledge could cure it.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.290
This is the medicine for shellskin.

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:51.920
I've written down how to synthesize it here.

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:55.020
Are you some kind of angel?

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:56.890
Hey, Nuts.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:59.530
He's cured everyone in town.

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:01.110
We should thank him.

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:05.230
That's right, Nuts. We should
 do something to thank him.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:08.510
Is there anything you want?

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:11.170
There is just one thing.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:13.980
My partner, Akaboshi Bisco.

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:17.160
I'd like you to free him 
and hand him over to me.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:19.110
Oh, Akaboshi?

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:20.870
Oh, yeah, he was with you, huh?

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:23.370
The two of them look 
nothing alike, so I forgot.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.480
Well, it's what our savior wants.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:26.790
So why not?

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:27.730
We can't!

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:31.920
If we don't secure weapons using
 the 800,000-sol reward for him,

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:36.450
the school of flying blowfish will 
come and devour this whole town!

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:40.190
If there's nothing else, then we're done here.

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:45.430
It's the blowfish!

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:47.570
The blowfish are here!

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:53.950
But why? It's the middle of summer!

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:56.960
Because the abnormal weather 
this year meant less food for them.

00:16:57.470 --> 00:17:00.200
I'll shoot them from up top. You all stay here.

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:07.660
Damn it, we're out of bullets!

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:14.780
You okay, Kewpie?!

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:16.230
Nuts...

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:20.220
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:20.220
<b>Tetsujin Town</b>

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:19.940
There's so many of them.
We don't have enough weapons for this.

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:26.980
Nuts!

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:28.550
Kousuke!

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:48.170
Hey, turban shell brat! 
Do you see how to use a harpoon now?!

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:50.280
If it's a memento of your father's,

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:55.040
all the more reason to use it up
 and send it to him in the afterlife,

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:58.040
not decorate a wall with it and your grudges!

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:01.030
Akaboshi! How did you get free?!

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:05.310
That crap doesn't work on me.

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:07.920
Nor do those completely rusted bars.

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:13.050
Kousuke, I looked at that map 
of yours, but it's defective.

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:16.070
Huh? B-But that can't be!

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:19.570
It doesn't have any furigana 
over the station names.

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:22.760
W-Wait, you can't read kanji?

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:26.130
Let's do a trade! My bow for your info.

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:29.840
I'll fire one arrow for every station you
 can name on the Toubu Shirakaba Line.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.100
Huh?!

00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:34.930
Well, hurry up and start talking 
before your friends get eaten.

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:37.840
And go in order. 
You memorized them all, right?

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:41.260
O-Okay, got it. The first station 
on the Shirakaba Line is...

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:42.300
Kitsunezaka!

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:49.090
Come on! There's lots more blowfish out there!

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:51.730
Um, uh... the second station is...

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:52.530
Kagamiboshi!

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:54.970
The third one is Tsueoki!

00:18:54.970 --> 00:18:56.280
Hinariyama!

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:57.230
Kamekoshi!

00:18:57.230 --> 00:18:58.570
Shougaiwa!

00:18:58.570 --> 00:18:59.910
Kabutobashi!

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:00.700
Irio!

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.180
Jizounuki Kouen!

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:03.300
Hakujadai!

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:04.690
Tsurikubisaki!

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:05.900
Haebaoka!

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:08.580
Okay, just one left.

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:11.370
Th-The final station is...

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:12.410
Konakidani!

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:18.680
Wow!

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:20.400
He did it!

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:25.730
I'll never forget this day as long as I live!

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:27.940
You were incredible, dude!

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:34.630
If a Mushroom Keeper needs your help
 again in the future, help 'em out.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:38.060
That's how bonds and connections are formed.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:40.940
That's what my own mentor told me.

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:42.950
Yeah! Got it!

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:48.130
Actagawa!

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:50.410
Later, Kousuke!

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:59.550
Milo, enough detours! Let's go!

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:00.510
Yeah.

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.790
Please stay here.

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:07.960
This town needs you.

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:12.470
What this town needs is you, not me.

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:19.500
You have a kind heart capable of caring 
about others in this run-down world.

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:23.110
That's more than enough 
to qualify you as a doctor.

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:26.990
Hey, will we ever meet again?

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:28.520
You'll meet someone.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:31.920
Someone much more amazing than me.

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:35.930
Akaboshi!

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:40.410
You decided to hand it over in the end, huh?

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:44.290
Don't get the wrong idea! 
I was trying to kill you with it!

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:49.830
Why can't you just say, 
"Thank you for saving our town"?

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:52.440
Annoying brat. Christ.

00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:56.190
Just can't be honest, huh?

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:58.180
Seriously.

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:00.840
Wait, which of us do you mean?

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:08.270
So much for "I'm sure I took out 
the old man he's partners with."

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:11.210
What a completely useless jellyfish.

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:15.330
I decide to take a look around since
 there's no body, and I find this.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:21.300
Governor, we searched every inch of the
 tunnels, but didn't find him anywhere.

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:25.760
Hmm, I see. A wasted effort, then.

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:42.230
An experienced hunter 
doesn't run when he's chased.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:45.700
He tries to catch his foe off-guard
 and outmaneuver them.

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:52.710
Which is even more true when 
they're a veteran Mushroom Keeper.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:37.470
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:37.470
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.540 --> 00:23:29.330
There are many famous 
movies set in snowfields.

00:23:29.330 --> 00:23:31.630
The extreme cold makes for extreme drama...

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:35.400
Oh, come on. These guys will turn 
anything into an action flick.

00:23:35.400 --> 00:23:37.470
Next episode: "Companions and Prey."

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Companions and Prey</b>

00:23:37.480 --> 00:23:39.470
Careful you don't get burned.
